# fuzzzy_ui_kit consumer-guard allow-list — the_master_of_law
#
#   fvm dart run fuzzzy_ui_kit:guard lib --allow=.fuzzzy_guard_allow
#
# One `path:line` pin per line, each with a stated reason. A pin without a
# reason is how an allow-list rots into a whitelist (guard.dart:36).
#
# TWO THINGS THAT WILL BITE YOU:
#   1. Paths are relative to the SCANNED ROOT. These pins are written for
#      `guard lib`, so they start `src/…`. Scanning `lib/src/features/x`
#      instead makes every pin here a no-op.
#   2. Pins are line-exact. If a pinned line moves, the pin silently stops
#      matching and the violation comes back — which is the correct, loud
#      failure. Re-check this file whenever a pinned file is edited.
